<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE script:module PUBLIC "-//OpenOffice.org//DTD OfficeDocument 1.0//EN" "module.dtd">
<script:module xmlns:script="http://openoffice.org/2000/script" script:name="CopyInsert" script:language="StarBasic" script:moduleType="normal">&apos; =====================================================================
&apos;  CopyInsert - copy / cut / move and insert for Calc
&apos;  Environment: LibreOffice 26.8.1.1. Library CopyInsertLib, module CopyInsert
&apos;  (My Macros).
&apos; =====================================================================
&apos;
&apos;  WHAT IT DOES
&apos;  Adds copy/insert, cut/insert and move/insert for rows, columns and cells in
&apos;  Calc spreadsheets. They are available after selecting the source data
&apos;  (row(s), column(s) or cell(s)) and clicking the mouse right button.
&apos;  Move works like cut, but the source rows / columns / cells are kept and
&apos;  only their content is cleared: their formatting stays as it was.
&apos;
&apos;  SEVERAL ROWS OR COLUMNS (Ctrl SELECTION)
&apos;  Rows (or columns) selected with the Ctrl key, even if they are not next to each
&apos;  other, are used as one source: they are inserted one after the other, in sheet order,
&apos;  as one block of consecutive rows (columns). Example: rows 2 and 10 are selected and
&apos;  &quot;copy above&quot; is chosen on row 7: row 2 is copied to the new row 7, row 10 to the new
&apos;  row 8, and the old row 7 becomes row 9. The same for columns, and for copy, paste
&apos;  special, cut and move. Cells still take one range only.
&apos;
&apos;  SHEETS
&apos;  Right-click a sheet tab (or select several tabs with Ctrl or Shift first): &quot;Copy
&apos;  sheets and insert&quot; &gt; Before / After, then click the tab of the destination sheet (one
&apos;  click). The sheet that is already displayed has no tab change to detect: for it click
&apos;  any of its cells instead.
&apos;  The selected sheets are copied as one block, in sheet order, and inserted before
&apos;  (after) the destination sheet. The sheets are copied like cells are: each copy keeps
&apos;  its sheet properties (tab color, column widths, page style ...), then its cells are
&apos;  pasted from the source. A reference between two sheets of the block that is
&apos;  relative (no &quot;$&quot; before the sheet name) therefore points to the copy of that sheet.
&apos;  A reference to a sheet outside the block stays relative as well, as with any paste:
&apos;  it points to whatever sheet lies at the same distance from the copy (or gives
&apos;  #REF!). An absolute reference ($Sheet1.A1) is never changed. Add the &quot;$&quot; yourself if
&apos;  a reference must stay on a given sheet. One Undo step; afterwards only the first new
&apos;  sheet is selected (and after an Undo only the first source sheet), with the same
&apos;  cells / rows / columns highlighted as before the copy (a single cell only gets the
&apos;  cursor, it is not highlighted).
&apos;  The selected sheets must be consecutive (Shift+click on the tabs): a selection with
&apos;  gaps is refused with a message, because the relative references between the sheets
&apos;  would not follow the copies. The copies must go OUTSIDE the range of the selected
&apos;  sheets: before the first one or after the last one. A destination inside that range
&apos;  is refused with a message, because the references between the sheets of the block
&apos;  would be broken.
&apos;
&apos;  OPTIONS
&apos;  1) Right-click menus for cells, rows and columns, each with copy, paste
&apos;     special, cut and move submenus. The Edit menu has the same four
&apos;     submenus, which follow the selection (see HOW IT WORKS).
&apos;  2) Above / below for rows, to the left / to the right for columns, and all
&apos;     four directions for cells.
&apos;  3) Submenu keyboard letters (English): A (above), B (below), L (left), R (right).
&apos;     In French: A (au-dessus), E (en dessous), G (gauche), D (droite).
&apos;  4) Cut and move keep formulas intact in the target area.
&apos;  5) One Undo step per plain copy, cut or move. Paste special takes two
&apos;     (the insertion, then the paste). After each Undo the source is selected.
&apos;  6) Works for Calc spreadsheets only.
&apos;  6b) The Edit menu offers the sheet copy (Copy and insert &gt; Before / After, shown in
&apos;     the Above / Below slots) only while several sheet tabs are selected; with one
&apos;     sheet use the sheet tab menu.
&apos;  7) Automatic setup: the extension runs EnableMenu from a job triggered by the
&apos;     &quot;View Created&quot; event (nothing appears in Tools &gt; Customize &gt; Events) and
&apos;     registers the keyboard shortcuts below, so nothing has to be assigned
&apos;     by hand. Without the extension: Tools &gt; Customize &gt; Events, with &quot;Save In&quot;
&apos;     set to LibreOffice (not the current spreadsheet), assign
&apos;     CopyInsertLib &gt; CopyInsert &gt; EnableMenu to the event &quot;View Created&quot;.
&apos;  8) Keyboard shortcuts. The extension registers these for Calc. All of them insert
&apos;     before the destination (above for rows and cells, to the left for columns):
&apos;       Alt+C  StartCopyBefore          Alt+X  StartCutBefore
&apos;       Alt+M  StartMoveBefore          Alt+P  StartPasteSpecialBefore
&apos;     Others can be assigned in Tools &gt; Customize &gt; Keyboard, then Application
&apos;     Macros &gt; My Macros &gt; CopyInsertLib &gt; CopyInsert:
&apos;       StartCopy          copy and insert after (below / to the right)
&apos;       StartPasteSpecial  copy, paste special and insert after
&apos;       StartCut           cut and insert after
&apos;       StartMove          move and insert after
&apos;     The &quot;before&quot; versions (above / to the left) are StartCopyBefore,
&apos;     StartPasteSpecialBefore, StartCutBefore and StartMoveBefore. For cells,
&apos;     the direction-specific ones are StartCopyAbove / Below / Left / Right
&apos;     (same pattern for PasteSpecial, Cut and Move).
&apos;  9) Languages: English and French. The texts are in the files
&apos;     l10n/CopyInsert_xx.properties of the extension (CopyInsert_en_US is the
&apos;     default, CopyInsert_fr is French). The language follows the LibreOffice user
&apos;     interface language (Tools &gt; Options &gt; Language Settings &gt; Languages).
&apos;     A language without a file, or a key missing from a file, uses the English text.
&apos;     Run the macro ShowLanguage to see what was detected.
&apos; 10) Install the extension with Tools &gt; Extension Manager &gt; Add. Double-clicking
&apos;     the .oxt file can make LibreOffice ask to install it again after every restart.
&apos;
&apos;  ADDING A LANGUAGE (for example German, code &quot;de&quot;). This module does not change.
&apos;     Three files per language, plus their entries in the two index files:
&apos;     1) l10n/CopyInsert_de.properties: copy CopyInsert_en_US.properties and translate
&apos;        the values. Keep the keys and the &quot;~&quot; keyboard-letter marks (the letter after
&apos;        the &quot;~&quot; is the shortcut; the letters must be different inside a submenu).
&apos;        Write accents as \uXXXX: the files are read as ASCII. A country file such as
&apos;        CopyInsert_fr_CA is used before CopyInsert_fr for that country.
&apos;     2) registry/Addons_de.xcu: copy Addons_fr.xcu and translate the four menu titles
&apos;        of the Edit menu. Add the file to META-INF/manifest.xml.
&apos;     3) description/description_de.txt: the text shown in the Extension Manager. Add it
&apos;        to META-INF/manifest.xml and to description.xml (a &lt;src&gt; line and a &lt;name&gt; line).
&apos;     4) Optional: license/license_de.txt, with a &lt;license-text&gt; line in description.xml.
&apos;        Without it the English license is shown.
&apos;     See l10n/README.txt.
&apos;
&apos;  GOOD TO KNOW
&apos;  1) The clipboard is overwritten with the copied range, as with a normal copy.
&apos;  2) Options that change the size of the pasted data do not fit. Transpose
&apos;     would paste a different shape than the space that was made.
&apos;  3) After a paste special, the selection is whatever the dialog leaves, not
&apos;     the automatic selection of the pasted data done by copy, cut and move.
&apos;  4) Cut and move relocate the cells with their formulas, so there is no
&apos;     paste special variant for them.
&apos;  5) Destination inside the source: not blocked for paste special (the data is
&apos;     copied before anything is inserted). Plain copy, cut and move refuse it.
&apos;  6) Right-clicking a whole-sheet selection adds nothing, since a whole sheet
&apos;     cannot be used as a source.
&apos;  7) Copying a cell whose relative address is part of the source and ends up
&apos;     pointing before row 1 or column 1 gives #REF!. This is normal Calc behavior.
&apos;  8) Cancelling the paste special dialog leaves the empty rows / columns / cells
&apos;     in place. Press Ctrl+Z once to remove them.
&apos;  9) Two Undo steps for paste special: the insertion and the paste are separate.
&apos; 10) A multiple (Ctrl) selection must be made of complete rows only, or of complete
&apos;     columns only, on one sheet. With anything else (cells, rows mixed with columns)
&apos;     the menus are not offered. Ranges that touch or overlap are merged, and the
&apos;     source is always used in sheet order, not in the order it was selected.
&apos; 11) Several source ranges are one Undo step as well (two for paste special). After an
&apos;     Undo, all the source ranges are selected again.
&apos; 12) Cut with several ranges: every emptied source row (column) is removed once all the
&apos;     data has been moved, so the pasted block ends up higher (further left) by the size
&apos;     of the removed ranges that were above (to the left of) the destination.
&apos; 13) Paste special with several ranges relies on Calc itself, which pastes the ranges of
&apos;     a multiple selection of complete rows (columns) one after the other.
&apos;
&apos;  HOW IT WORKS
&apos;   - A context menu interceptor adds the entries (CMI_ functions). The sheet tab menu is
&apos;     recognized by its Rename Sheet entry and gets &quot;Copy sheets and insert&quot; after
&apos;     Move or Copy Sheet (AddSheetEntries).
&apos;   - Sheets: ArmSheetCopy saves the state &quot;SHEETS|0|before|0|0|firstSheet|1,2,5&quot; (the
&apos;     selected sheet indexes), opens the same destination window and also listens to
&apos;     the sheet changes (AS_activeSpreadsheetChanged): a click on a sheet tab closes
&apos;     the window and gives the destination at once, while a click on a cell still ends
&apos;     in RS_done. Both then call PerformSheetCopy: copyByName for every sheet (all the copies exist first), then
&apos;     copyRange of each source used area onto its copy, which gives the usual paste
&apos;     behavior to the references between sheets. Undo: one step, first source sheet selected.
&apos;   - The Edit menu entries come from registry/Addons.xcu (merged after Paste
&apos;     Special, Calc only). A Python protocol handler (python/CopyInsertEditMenu.py)
&apos;     answers LibreOffice&apos;s status request each time Edit opens: it enables only
&apos;     the directions that fit the selection (rows: above / below, columns: left /
&apos;     right, cells: all four) and adds the word rows / columns / cells (keys
&apos;     k.rows, k.columns, k.cells). The four submenu titles are fixed text:
&apos;     LibreOffice never asks for their status. A click runs the matching
&apos;     Start... macro below.
&apos;   - ArmPendingEx saves the source in a temporary DOCUMENT PROPERTY
&apos;     (CopyInsertState = mode|cut 0/1/2|before|special|right|sheet|ranges|timestamp,
&apos;     where &quot;cut&quot; is 0 = copy, 1 = cut, 2 = move, and ranges is a list such as
&apos;     c1,r1,c2,r2;c1,r1,c2,r2 : one entry per source range) and opens startRangeSelection.
&apos;     RS_done reads the click and runs the operation.
&apos;   - PerformInsert: insert room for all the source ranges together, then copyRange (copy)
&apos;     or moveRange (cut / move) for each range in turn. Cut deletes the emptied source,
&apos;     move keeps it (bRemove flag).
&apos;   - A selection is read by ReadSelection: a single range, or the ranges of a Ctrl
&apos;     selection (a SheetCellRanges object, which has no RangeAddress property).
&apos;     Sets of ranges are Long arrays aR(field, index), fields 0..3 = c1, r1, c2, r2.
&apos;   - PerformPasteSpecial: copy to the clipboard, insert room, open Paste Special.
&apos;   - The Undo listener (UM_) reselects the source after an Undo, using the
&apos;     properties CopyInsertUndo and CopyInsertPSSrc and the Undo title prefix
&apos;     (translated, see UndoPrefix).
&apos;   - All texts come from Txt(&quot;key&quot;): the properties file of the active language,
&apos;     then the English one (InitRes, PickLocale, ResolveIn).
&apos;
&apos;  THINGS LEARNED THE HARD WAY
&apos;   - XSelectionChangeListener never fired. Module-level variables are reset
&apos;     between events, so the state lives in the document property.
&apos;   - Menu item properties must be set with setPropertyValue (Text, SubContainer).
&apos;   - Duplicate interceptors pile up when the module is edited. The guard checks
&apos;     the labels of every language (IsOurLabel). After any edit, close and
&apos;     reopen the document.
&apos;   - Do not name a variable sTop (it collides with Stop). Basic is case-insensitive.
&apos;   - The destination is passed as plain numbers, not as an address object.
&apos;   - The &quot;: area&quot; text in the destination window comes from LibreOffice and
&apos;     cannot be changed. Starting the window with an empty range (InitialValue)
&apos;     was tried and reverted. The highlight of the source area on other sheets
&apos;     is also LibreOffice&apos;s own behavior.
&apos;   - Paste special is two Undo steps. The second one is recognized by checking
&apos;     the top of the Undo stack.
&apos;   - The string resource service reads the .properties files as ASCII (write accents
&apos;     as \uXXXX). It does not fall back by itself: a missing key raises an error, and
&apos;     a language without a file gets some other file. InitRes therefore picks the file
&apos;     (PickLocale) and Txt falls back to English key by key.
&apos;   - Paste special: .uno:PasteSpecial is ignored if LibreOffice has not yet processed the
&apos;     clipboard change caused by .uno:Copy (seen on the first use in a session). The
&apos;     dispatch normally blocks while the dialog is open, so a call that returns at once
&apos;     is retried after letting the event loop run (OpenPasteSpecial).
&apos;   - A keyboard shortcut label appears next to a menu entry only if the entry runs the
&apos;     very macro the shortcut is bound to (the ...Before macros): see AddCellSubmenu.
&apos;   - License fallback in description.xml: default-license-id must name a license-text
&apos;     that has that license-id, or installing with an unlisted UI language fails with
&apos;     &quot;Could not obtain path to license&quot;.
&apos;   - In an error handler, read Error$ and Erl FIRST: calling a function that has
&apos;     its own error handling (like Txt) can reset them.
&apos; =====================================================================

Option Explicit

&apos; ---------- Settings ----------
Const MACRO_BASE = &quot;vnd.sun.star.script:CopyInsertLib.CopyInsert.&quot;
Const MACRO_TAIL = &quot;?language=Basic&amp;location=application&quot;
&apos; True: menus use submenus / False: flat lists of entries
Const USE_SUBMENUS = True
&apos; Default direction for cells when StartCopy / StartCut / StartMove / StartPasteSpecial are used
&apos; (for example from a keyboard shortcut): True = shift down, False = shift right
Const CELLS_SHIFT_DOWN = True
Const STATE_NAME = &quot;CopyInsertState&quot;
&apos; Used to reselect the source after an Undo
Const UNDO_NAME = &quot;CopyInsertUndo&quot;           &apos; source for the undo of the insertion
Const PSSRC_NAME = &quot;CopyInsertPSSrc&quot;         &apos; paste special: source as it sits after the insertion

&apos; ---------- Translations ----------
&apos; The texts are in the files l10n/CopyInsert_xx.properties of the extension
&apos; (CopyInsert_en_US.properties is the default). Leave L10N_DIR empty to use the l10n
&apos; folder of the installed extension. To work on this module in My Macros without the
&apos; extension, put the URL of a folder holding the files here, for example
&apos; &quot;file:///home/me/CopyInsert/l10n/&quot;.
Const L10N_DIR = &quot;&quot;
Const L10N_BASE = &quot;CopyInsert&quot;
Const EXT_ID = &quot;org.libreoffice.extension.copyinsert&quot;

&apos; ---------- State used only while PerformInsert runs ----------
Private oInterceptor As Object
Private oUndoListener As Object
Private oSelListener As Object
Private oActListener As Object            &apos; sheets: tells which sheet tab was clicked
Private oSrcDoc As Object
Private oSrcAddr As Variant      &apos; first source range (the only one for cells)
Private aSrcRanges As Variant    &apos; all source ranges: aR(field, index), see ReadSelection
Private sSrcMode As String
Private bCutMode As Boolean
Private bMoveMode As Boolean
Private bBeforeMode As Boolean
Private bSpecialMode As Boolean
Private bShiftRight As Boolean
Private oResCur As Object       &apos; texts of the user interface language
Private oResEn As Object        &apos; English texts (for a missing language or key)
Private bCurOK As Boolean       &apos; oResCur holds usable texts
Private bEnOK As Boolean        &apos; oResEn holds usable texts
Private bResInit As Boolean


Function IsCalcDoc(oDoc As Object) As Boolean
    IsCalcDoc = False
    If IsNull(oDoc) Or IsEmpty(oDoc) Then Exit Function
    IsCalcDoc = oDoc.supportsService(&quot;com.sun.star.sheet.SpreadsheetDocument&quot;)
End Function


&apos;=====================================================================
&apos;  0a. Source ranges: one range, or several (Ctrl selection)
&apos;      A set of ranges is a Long array aR(field, index) with the fields
&apos;      0 = first column, 1 = first row, 2 = last column, 3 = last row.
&apos;=====================================================================
&apos; Reads a selection as a set of ranges. nSheet receives the sheet index.
&apos; Returns Empty if the selection is not made of cell ranges, or spreads over several sheets.
Function ReadSelection(oSel As Variant, nSheet As Long) As Variant
    Dim aAddr As Variant, aOut() As Long, i As Long, n As Long, oA As Object

    ReadSelection = Empty
    On Error GoTo SelFail
    If IsNull(oSel) Or IsEmpty(oSel) Then Exit Function
    If HasUnoInterfaces(oSel, &quot;com.sun.star.sheet.XCellRangeAddressable&quot;) Then
        oA = oSel.RangeAddress
        nSheet = oA.Sheet
        ReDim aOut(3, 0)
        aOut(0, 0) = oA.StartColumn : aOut(1, 0) = oA.StartRow
        aOut(2, 0) = oA.EndColumn   : aOut(3, 0) = oA.EndRow
    ElseIf HasUnoInterfaces(oSel, &quot;com.sun.star.sheet.XSheetCellRanges&quot;) Then
        aAddr = oSel.getRangeAddresses()
        n = UBound(aAddr) + 1
        If n &lt; 1 Then Exit Function
        nSheet = aAddr(0).Sheet
        ReDim aOut(3, n - 1)
        For i = 0 To n - 1
            If aAddr(i).Sheet &lt;&gt; nSheet Then Exit Function
            aOut(0, i) = aAddr(i).StartColumn : aOut(1, i) = aAddr(i).StartRow
            aOut(2, i) = aAddr(i).EndColumn   : aOut(3, i) = aAddr(i).EndRow
        Next i
    Else
        Exit Function
    End If
    ReadSelection = aOut
    Exit Function

SelFail:
    ReadSelection = Empty
End Function

&apos; &quot;WHOLE&quot; (a whole sheet is part of it), &quot;ROWS&quot; (all complete rows), &quot;COLS&quot; (all complete
&apos; columns), &quot;CELLS&quot; (one range of cells) or &quot;MIXED&quot; (anything else: not supported)
Function KindOfRanges(oDoc As Object, nSheet As Long, aR As Variant) As String
    Dim oSheet As Object, nCols As Long, nRows As Long, i As Long, n As Long
    Dim bAllRows As Boolean, bAllCols As Boolean, bFullR As Boolean, bFullC As Boolean

    oSheet = oDoc.Sheets.getByIndex(nSheet)
    nCols = oSheet.Columns.Count
    nRows = oSheet.Rows.Count
    n = UBound(aR, 2) + 1
    bAllRows = True
    bAllCols = True
    For i = 0 To n - 1
        bFullR = (aR(0, i) = 0 And aR(2, i) = nCols - 1)
        bFullC = (aR(1, i) = 0 And aR(3, i) = nRows - 1)
        If bFullR And bFullC Then
            KindOfRanges = &quot;WHOLE&quot;
            Exit Function
        End If
        If Not bFullR Then bAllRows = False
        If Not bFullC Then bAllCols = False
    Next i
    If bAllRows Then
        KindOfRanges = &quot;ROWS&quot;
    ElseIf bAllCols Then
        KindOfRanges = &quot;COLS&quot;
    ElseIf n = 1 Then
        KindOfRanges = &quot;CELLS&quot;
    Else
        KindOfRanges = &quot;MIXED&quot;
    End If
End Function

&apos; Sorts complete rows (nS = 1) or complete columns (nS = 0) in sheet order and merges the
&apos; ones that touch or overlap
Function NormalizeRanges(aR As Variant, nS As Long) As Variant
    Dim nE As Long, n As Long, i As Long, j As Long, k As Long, m As Long, t As Long
    Dim aOut() As Long, bJoin As Boolean

    nE = nS + 2
    n = UBound(aR, 2) + 1
    For i = 1 To n - 1                     &apos; insertion sort on the first row (column)
        j = i
        Do While j &gt; 0
            If aR(nS, j - 1) &lt;= aR(nS, j) Then Exit Do
            For k = 0 To 3
                t = aR(k, j - 1) : aR(k, j - 1) = aR(k, j) : aR(k, j) = t
            Next k
            j = j - 1
        Loop
    Next i

    ReDim aOut(3, n - 1)
    m = 0
    For i = 0 To n - 1
        bJoin = False                       &apos; (And does not short-circuit in Basic)
        If m &gt; 0 Then
            If aR(nS, i) &lt;= aOut(nE, m - 1) + 1 Then bJoin = True
        End If
        If bJoin Then
            If aR(nE, i) &gt; aOut(nE, m - 1) Then aOut(nE, m - 1) = aR(nE, i)
        Else
            For k = 0 To 3
                aOut(k, m) = aR(k, i)
            Next k
            m = m + 1
        End If
    Next i
    ReDim Preserve aOut(3, m - 1)
    NormalizeRanges = aOut
End Function

&apos; Total number of rows (nS = 1) or columns (nS = 0) of a set of ranges
Function TotalSize(aR As Variant, nS As Long) As Long
    Dim i As Long, n As Long
    n = 0
    For i = 0 To UBound(aR, 2)
        n = n + aR(nS + 2, i) - aR(nS, i) + 1
    Next i
    TotalSize = n
End Function

Function CopyRanges(aR As Variant) As Variant
    Dim aOut() As Long, i As Long, k As Long
    ReDim aOut(3, UBound(aR, 2))
    For i = 0 To UBound(aR, 2)
        For k = 0 To 3
            aOut(k, i) = aR(k, i)
        Next k
    Next i
    CopyRanges = aOut
End Function

&apos; &quot;c1,r1,c2,r2;c1,r1,c2,r2&quot; (no &quot;|&quot;: it goes inside the saved states)
Function RangesToString(aR As Variant) As String
    Dim s As String, i As Long
    s = &quot;&quot;
    For i = 0 To UBound(aR, 2)
        If i &gt; 0 Then s = s &amp; &quot;;&quot;
        s = s &amp; aR(0, i) &amp; &quot;,&quot; &amp; aR(1, i) &amp; &quot;,&quot; &amp; aR(2, i) &amp; &quot;,&quot; &amp; aR(3, i)
    Next i
    RangesToString = s
End Function

Function StringToRanges(s As String) As Variant
    Dim p() As String, q() As String, aOut() As Long, i As Long, k As Long
    p = Split(s, &quot;;&quot;)
    ReDim aOut(3, UBound(p))
    For i = 0 To UBound(p)
        q = Split(p(i), &quot;,&quot;)
        For k = 0 To 3
            aOut(k, i) = CLng(q(k))
        Next k
    Next i
    StringToRanges = aOut
End Function

&apos; What to select to show or copy a set of ranges: a range, or the ranges of a Ctrl selection
Function BuildSelection(oDoc As Object, nSheet As Long, aR As Variant) As Object
    Dim oSheet As Object, oRanges As Object, i As Long
    Dim oA As New com.sun.star.table.CellRangeAddress

    oSheet = oDoc.Sheets.getByIndex(nSheet)
    If UBound(aR, 2) = 0 Then
        BuildSelection = oSheet.getCellRangeByPosition(aR(0, 0), aR(1, 0), aR(2, 0), aR(3, 0))
        Exit Function
    End If
    oRanges = oDoc.createInstance(&quot;com.sun.star.sheet.SheetCellRanges&quot;)
    oA.Sheet = nSheet
    For i = 0 To UBound(aR, 2)
        oA.StartColumn = aR(0, i) : oA.StartRow = aR(1, i)
        oA.EndColumn = aR(2, i)   : oA.EndRow = aR(3, i)
        oRanges.addRangeAddress(oA, False)
    Next i
    BuildSelection = oRanges
End Function


&apos;=====================================================================
&apos;  0. Languages: detection and texts
&apos;=====================================================================
&apos; Reads the LibreOffice user interface locale (for example &quot;fr-FR&quot;).
&apos; Returns &quot;&quot; if it cannot be read.
Function ReadUILocale() As String
    Dim oProv As Object, oNode As Object, sLoc As String
    Dim aArgs(0) As New com.sun.star.beans.PropertyValue

    ReadUILocale = &quot;&quot;
    On Error GoTo LangFail
    oProv = createUnoService(&quot;com.sun.star.configuration.ConfigurationProvider&quot;)
    aArgs(0).Name = &quot;nodepath&quot;
    aArgs(0).Value = &quot;/org.openoffice.Setup/L10N&quot;
    oNode = oProv.createInstanceWithArguments(&quot;com.sun.star.configuration.ConfigurationAccess&quot;, aArgs())
    sLoc = oNode.getByName(&quot;ooLocale&quot;)
    If Len(sLoc) = 0 Then sLoc = oNode.getByName(&quot;ooSetupSystemLocale&quot;)
    ReadUILocale = sLoc
    Exit Function

LangFail:
    ReadUILocale = &quot;&quot;
End Function

&apos; Splits a locale such as &quot;fr-FR&quot; or &quot;zh-Hans-CN&quot; into a Locale structure
Function ToLocale(sLoc As String) As Variant
    Dim aLoc As New com.sun.star.lang.Locale
    Dim a() As String
    a = Split(Replace(sLoc, &quot;_&quot;, &quot;-&quot;), &quot;-&quot;)
    If UBound(a) &gt;= 0 Then aLoc.Language = LCase(a(0))
    If UBound(a) &gt;= 1 Then
        If Len(a(UBound(a))) = 2 Then aLoc.Country = UCase(a(UBound(a)))
    End If
    ToLocale = aLoc
End Function

&apos; URL (with a closing slash) of the folder holding the translation files,
&apos; or &quot;&quot; if it cannot be found
Function L10nFolder() As String
    Dim sUrl As String, oPip As Object
    L10nFolder = &quot;&quot;
    sUrl = L10N_DIR
    If sUrl = &quot;&quot; Then
        On Error GoTo NoFolder
        oPip = GetDefaultContext().getValueByName( _
            &quot;/singletons/com.sun.star.deployment.PackageInformationProvider&quot;)
        sUrl = oPip.getPackageLocation(EXT_ID)
        If sUrl &lt;&gt; &quot;&quot; Then sUrl = sUrl &amp; &quot;/l10n&quot;
    End If
    If sUrl &lt;&gt; &quot;&quot; And Right(sUrl, 1) &lt;&gt; &quot;/&quot; Then sUrl = sUrl &amp; &quot;/&quot;
    L10nFolder = sUrl
    Exit Function

NoFolder:
    L10nFolder = &quot;&quot;
End Function

&apos; Opens the translation files of the folder (Empty if that fails)
Function OpenRes(sFolder As String, aLoc As Variant) As Variant
    Dim oHandler As Object, aArgs As Variant
    On Error GoTo OpenFail
    oHandler = createUnoService(&quot;com.sun.star.task.InteractionHandler&quot;)
    aArgs = Array(sFolder, True, aLoc, L10N_BASE, &quot;&quot;, oHandler)
    OpenRes = GetProcessServiceManager().createInstanceWithArgumentsAndContext( _
        &quot;com.sun.star.resource.StringResourceWithLocation&quot;, aArgs, GetDefaultContext())
    Exit Function

OpenFail:
    OpenRes = Empty
End Function

&apos; Selects, among the files found, the best one for the wanted locale: same language and
&apos; country, then the language alone (CopyInsert_fr), then the same language with another
&apos; country. If nothing fits, the current locale is left as it is.
Sub PickLocale(oRes As Object, aWant As Variant)
    Dim aList As Variant, i As Long, nBest As Long, nTop As Long, nScore As Long
    aList = oRes.getLocales()
    nBest = -1
    nTop = 0
    For i = 0 To UBound(aList)
        nScore = 0
        If aList(i).Language = aWant.Language Then
            nScore = 1
            If aList(i).Country = &quot;&quot; Then nScore = 2
            If aWant.Country &lt;&gt; &quot;&quot; And aList(i).Country = aWant.Country Then nScore = 3
        End If
        If nScore &gt; nTop Then
            nTop = nScore
            nBest = i
        End If
    Next i
    If nBest &gt;= 0 Then oRes.setCurrentLocale(aList(nBest), False)
End Sub

&apos; Opens the English texts and, if the user interface language has a file, its texts.
&apos; LibreOffice does not fall back by itself (a missing key is an error, and an unknown
&apos; language gets some other file), so the choice is made here.
Sub InitRes()
    Dim sFolder As String, aWant As Variant, aCur As Variant, vRes As Variant
    If bResInit Then Exit Sub
    bResInit = True
    bEnOK = False
    bCurOK = False
    sFolder = L10nFolder()
    If sFolder = &quot;&quot; Then Exit Sub
    vRes = OpenRes(sFolder, ToLocale(&quot;en-US&quot;))
    If Not IsEmpty(vRes) Then
        oResEn = vRes
        bEnOK = True
    End If
    aWant = ToLocale(ReadUILocale())
    If aWant.Language = &quot;&quot; Then Exit Sub
    vRes = OpenRes(sFolder, aWant)
    If IsEmpty(vRes) Then Exit Sub
    oResCur = vRes
    PickLocale oResCur, aWant
    aCur = oResCur.getCurrentLocale()
    &apos; English needs no second set of texts
    If aCur.Language = aWant.Language Then
        If Not (aCur.Language = &quot;en&quot; And aCur.Country = &quot;US&quot;) Then bCurOK = True
    End If
End Sub

&apos; Text of a key in the active language (bCur = True) or in English (False), &quot;&quot; if not there
Function ResolveIn(bCur As Boolean, sKey As String) As String
    ResolveIn = &quot;&quot;
    On Error GoTo NotFound
    If bCur Then
        If bCurOK Then ResolveIn = oResCur.resolveString(sKey)
    Else
        If bEnOK Then ResolveIn = oResEn.resolveString(sKey)
    End If
    Exit Function

NotFound:
    ResolveIn = &quot;&quot;
End Function

&apos; Run it to check what was detected
Sub ShowLanguage()
    Dim sFile As String, aCur As Variant
    InitRes
    sFile = &quot;English (CopyInsert_en_US)&quot;
    If bCurOK Then
        aCur = oResCur.getCurrentLocale()
        sFile = L10N_BASE &amp; &quot;_&quot; &amp; aCur.Language
        If aCur.Country &lt;&gt; &quot;&quot; Then sFile = sFile &amp; &quot;_&quot; &amp; aCur.Country
    End If
    MsgBox &quot;UI locale: &quot; &amp; ReadUILocale() &amp; Chr(10) &amp; _
           &quot;Folder: &quot; &amp; L10nFolder() &amp; Chr(10) &amp; _
           &quot;Language file used: &quot; &amp; sFile &amp; Chr(10) &amp; _
           Txt(&quot;m.copy.cells&quot;)
End Sub

&apos; Text of a key in the active language (falls back to English, then to the key itself)
Function Txt(sKey As String) As String
    Dim s As String
    InitRes
    s = ResolveIn(True, sKey)
    If s = &quot;&quot; Then s = ResolveIn(False, sKey)
    If s = &quot;&quot; Then s = sKey
    Txt = s
End Function

&apos; Start of the Undo titles of our operations (the step title is prefix + kind)
Function UndoPrefix() As String
    UndoPrefix = Txt(&quot;undo.prefix&quot;)
End Function


&apos;=====================================================================
&apos;  1. Enable the context-menu interceptor and the Undo listener
&apos;=====================================================================
Sub EnableMenu()
    Dim oCtrl As Object
    If Not IsCalcDoc(ThisComponent) Then Exit Sub
    If IsNull(oInterceptor) Then
        oInterceptor = CreateUnoListener(&quot;CMI_&quot;, &quot;com.sun.star.ui.XContextMenuInterceptor&quot;)
    End If
    oCtrl = ThisComponent.CurrentController
    oCtrl.releaseContextMenuInterceptor(oInterceptor)   &apos; avoid duplicates
    oCtrl.registerContextMenuInterceptor(oInterceptor)

    &apos; --- Undo listener: reselects the source after an Undo ---
    On Error Resume Next
    If IsNull(oUndoListener) Then
        oUndoListener = CreateUnoListener(&quot;UM_&quot;, &quot;com.sun.star.document.XUndoManagerListener&quot;)
    End If
    ThisComponent.UndoManager.removeUndoManagerListener(oUndoListener)
    ThisComponent.UndoManager.addUndoManagerListener(oUndoListener)
    On Error GoTo 0
End Sub

Sub AddMenuItem(oMenu As Object, nPos As Long, sText As String, sMacro As String)
    Dim oItem As Object
    oItem = oMenu.createInstance(&quot;com.sun.star.ui.ActionTrigger&quot;)
    oItem.setPropertyValue(&quot;Text&quot;, sText)
    oItem.setPropertyValue(&quot;CommandURL&quot;, MACRO_BASE &amp; sMacro &amp; MACRO_TAIL)
    oMenu.insertByIndex(nPos, oItem)
End Sub

Sub AddMenuSeparator(oMenu As Object, nPos As Long)
    Dim oSep As Object
    oSep = oMenu.createInstance(&quot;com.sun.star.ui.ActionTriggerSeparator&quot;)
    oSep.setPropertyValue(&quot;SeparatorType&quot;, com.sun.star.ui.ActionTriggerSeparatorType.LINE)
    oMenu.insertByIndex(nPos, oSep)
End Sub

&apos; Submenu for cells: above / below / left / right
Sub AddCellSubmenu(oMenu As Object, nPos As Long, sTitle As String, sPrefix As String)
    Dim oSub As Object, oItem As Object
    oSub = oMenu.createInstance(&quot;com.sun.star.ui.ActionTriggerContainer&quot;)
    &apos; The entry that matches the keyboard shortcut (Alt+C, Alt+P, Alt+X, Alt+M) runs the
    &apos; ...Before macro, which does the same as ...Above (or ...Left if CELLS_SHIFT_DOWN is
    &apos; False). LibreOffice shows the shortcut next to an entry only if it runs that very macro.
    If CELLS_SHIFT_DOWN Then
        AddMenuItem oSub, 0, Txt(&quot;dir.above&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, sPrefix &amp; &quot;Before&quot;
        AddMenuItem oSub, 1, Txt(&quot;dir.below&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, sPrefix &amp; &quot;Below&quot;
        AddMenuItem oSub, 2, Txt(&quot;dir.left&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, sPrefix &amp; &quot;Left&quot;
        AddMenuItem oSub, 3, Txt(&quot;dir.right&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, sPrefix &amp; &quot;Right&quot;
    Else
        AddMenuItem oSub, 0, Txt(&quot;dir.above&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, sPrefix &amp; &quot;Above&quot;
        AddMenuItem oSub, 1, Txt(&quot;dir.below&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, sPrefix &amp; &quot;Below&quot;
        AddMenuItem oSub, 2, Txt(&quot;dir.left&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, sPrefix &amp; &quot;Before&quot;
        AddMenuItem oSub, 3, Txt(&quot;dir.right&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, sPrefix &amp; &quot;Right&quot;
    End If

    oItem = oMenu.createInstance(&quot;com.sun.star.ui.ActionTrigger&quot;)
    oItem.setPropertyValue(&quot;Text&quot;, sTitle)
    oItem.setPropertyValue(&quot;SubContainer&quot;, oSub)
    oMenu.insertByIndex(nPos, oItem)
End Sub

&apos; Submenu for rows / columns: first entry = &quot;before&quot; (above / left), second = &quot;after&quot; (below / right)
Sub AddBeforeAfterSubmenu(oMenu As Object, nPos As Long, sTitle As String, _
                          sBeforeTxt As String, sAfterTxt As String, _
                          sBeforeMacro As String, sAfterMacro As String)
    Dim oSub As Object, oItem As Object
    oSub = oMenu.createInstance(&quot;com.sun.star.ui.ActionTriggerContainer&quot;)
    AddMenuItem oSub, 0, sBeforeTxt &amp; &quot;...&quot;, sBeforeMacro
    AddMenuItem oSub, 1, sAfterTxt &amp; &quot;...&quot;, sAfterMacro

    oItem = oMenu.createInstance(&quot;com.sun.star.ui.ActionTrigger&quot;)
    oItem.setPropertyValue(&quot;Text&quot;, sTitle)
    oItem.setPropertyValue(&quot;SubContainer&quot;, oSub)
    oMenu.insertByIndex(nPos, oItem)
End Sub

&apos; True if the text is the title of one of our submenu parents (active language or English)
Function IsOurLabel(sTxt As String) As Boolean
    Dim aKinds As Variant, aActs As Variant
    Dim j As Long, k As Long, sKey As String
    IsOurLabel = False
    If Len(sTxt) = 0 Then Exit Function
    InitRes
    aKinds = Array(&quot;cells&quot;, &quot;rows&quot;, &quot;columns&quot;, &quot;sheets&quot;)
    aActs = Array(&quot;copy&quot;, &quot;paste&quot;, &quot;cut&quot;, &quot;move&quot;)
    For j = 0 To UBound(aKinds)
        For k = 0 To UBound(aActs)
            sKey = &quot;m.&quot; &amp; aActs(k) &amp; &quot;.&quot; &amp; aKinds(j)
            If sTxt = ResolveIn(True, sKey) Or sTxt = ResolveIn(False, sKey) Then
                IsOurLabel = True
                Exit Function
            End If
        Next k
    Next j
End Function

&apos; True if one of our entries (flat item or submenu parent) is already in the menu
Function MenuHasOurEntries(oMenu As Object) As Boolean
    Dim i As Long, oItem As Object, sCmd As String, sTxt As String
    MenuHasOurEntries = False
    On Error Resume Next
    For i = 0 To oMenu.Count - 1
        oItem = oMenu.getByIndex(i)
        sCmd = &quot;&quot; : sTxt = &quot;&quot;
        sCmd = oItem.getPropertyValue(&quot;CommandURL&quot;)
        sTxt = oItem.getPropertyValue(&quot;Text&quot;)
        If Left(sCmd, Len(MACRO_BASE)) = MACRO_BASE Then
            MenuHasOurEntries = True
            Exit For
        End If
        If IsOurLabel(sTxt) Then
            MenuHasOurEntries = True
            Exit For
        End If
    Next i
End Function

&apos; True if the menu is the one of the sheet tabs (it has Rename Sheet)
Function IsSheetTabMenu(oMenu As Object) As Boolean
    Dim i As Long, oItem As Object, sCmd As String
    IsSheetTabMenu = False
    On Error Resume Next
    For i = 0 To oMenu.Count - 1
        oItem = oMenu.getByIndex(i)
        sCmd = &quot;&quot;
        sCmd = oItem.getPropertyValue(&quot;CommandURL&quot;)
        If sCmd = &quot;.uno:RenameTable&quot; Then
            IsSheetTabMenu = True
            Exit For
        End If
    Next i
End Function

&apos; The sheets of the selection (sheet tabs selected with Ctrl or Shift give a selection
&apos; over several sheets), as a Long array in sheet order. Empty if there is none.
Function ReadSheetSelection(oSel As Variant) As Variant
    Dim aAddr As Variant, aOut() As Long, i As Long, j As Long, n As Long
    Dim bKnown As Boolean, nTmp As Long

    ReadSheetSelection = Empty
    On Error GoTo SelFail
    If IsNull(oSel) Or IsEmpty(oSel) Then Exit Function
    If HasUnoInterfaces(oSel, &quot;com.sun.star.sheet.XCellRangeAddressable&quot;) Then
        ReDim aOut(0)
        aOut(0) = oSel.RangeAddress.Sheet
        ReadSheetSelection = aOut
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Not HasUnoInterfaces(oSel, &quot;com.sun.star.sheet.XSheetCellRanges&quot;) Then Exit Function
    aAddr = oSel.getRangeAddresses()
    If UBound(aAddr) &lt; 0 Then Exit Function
    ReDim aOut(UBound(aAddr))
    n = 0
    For i = 0 To UBound(aAddr)
        bKnown = False
        For j = 0 To n - 1
            If aOut(j) = aAddr(i).Sheet Then bKnown = True
        Next j
        If Not bKnown Then
            aOut(n) = aAddr(i).Sheet
            n = n + 1
        End If
    Next i
    ReDim Preserve aOut(n - 1)
    For i = 0 To n - 2                       &apos; sheet order
        For j = i + 1 To n - 1
            If aOut(j) &lt; aOut(i) Then
                nTmp = aOut(i) : aOut(i) = aOut(j) : aOut(j) = nTmp
            End If
        Next j
    Next i
    ReadSheetSelection = aOut
    Exit Function

SelFail:
    ReadSheetSelection = Empty
End Function

&apos; The highlighted ranges of the selection that lie on sheet nSheet, as &quot;c1,r1,c2,r2;...&quot; (a
&apos; row, a column or cells). If none lies on that sheet, the first range whatever its sheet.
&apos; &quot;&quot; if the selection cannot be read.
Function SelectedRangesOnSheet(oSel As Variant, nSheet As Long) As String
    Dim aAddr As Variant, i As Long, sOut As String

    SelectedRangesOnSheet = &quot;&quot;
    On Error GoTo RangesFail
    If HasUnoInterfaces(oSel, &quot;com.sun.star.sheet.XCellRangeAddressable&quot;) Then
        aAddr = Array(oSel.RangeAddress)
    ElseIf HasUnoInterfaces(oSel, &quot;com.sun.star.sheet.XSheetCellRanges&quot;) Then
        aAddr = oSel.getRangeAddresses()
    Else
        Exit Function
    End If
    If UBound(aAddr) &lt; 0 Then Exit Function
    sOut = &quot;&quot;
    For i = 0 To UBound(aAddr)
        If aAddr(i).Sheet = nSheet Then
            If sOut &lt;&gt; &quot;&quot; Then sOut = sOut &amp; &quot;;&quot;
            sOut = sOut &amp; aAddr(i).StartColumn &amp; &quot;,&quot; &amp; aAddr(i).StartRow &amp; &quot;,&quot; &amp; _
                   aAddr(i).EndColumn &amp; &quot;,&quot; &amp; aAddr(i).EndRow
        End If
    Next i
    If sOut = &quot;&quot; Then
        sOut = aAddr(0).StartColumn &amp; &quot;,&quot; &amp; aAddr(0).StartRow &amp; &quot;,&quot; &amp; _
               aAddr(0).EndColumn &amp; &quot;,&quot; &amp; aAddr(0).EndRow
    End If
    SelectedRangesOnSheet = sOut
    Exit Function

RangesFail:
    SelectedRangesOnSheet = &quot;&quot;
End Function

&apos; Adds &quot;Copy sheets and insert&quot; (before / after) to the sheet tab menu, after Move or Copy
&apos; Sheet. Returns False (nothing added) when the selected sheets cannot be read.
Function AddSheetEntries(oMenu As Object, oSel As Variant) As Boolean
    Dim i As Long, nPos As Long, oItem As Object, sCmd As String, sCopy As String

    AddSheetEntries = False
    If IsEmpty(ReadSheetSelection(oSel)) Then Exit Function

    nPos = oMenu.Count
    On Error Resume Next
    For i = 0 To oMenu.Count - 1
        oItem = oMenu.getByIndex(i)
        sCmd = &quot;&quot;
        sCmd = oItem.getPropertyValue(&quot;CommandURL&quot;)
        If sCmd = &quot;.uno:Move&quot; Then
            nPos = i + 1
            Exit For
        End If
    Next i
    On Error GoTo 0

    sCopy = Txt(&quot;m.copy.sheets&quot;)
    If USE_SUBMENUS Then
        AddBeforeAfterSubmenu oMenu, nPos, sCopy, Txt(&quot;dir.before&quot;), Txt(&quot;dir.after&quot;), _
                              &quot;StartCopySheetsBefore&quot;, &quot;StartCopySheets&quot;
    Else
        AddMenuItem oMenu, nPos, sCopy &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; Txt(&quot;low.before&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartCopySheetsBefore&quot;
        AddMenuItem oMenu, nPos + 1, sCopy &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; Txt(&quot;low.after&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartCopySheets&quot;
    End If
    AddSheetEntries = True
End Function

Function CMI_notifyContextMenuExecute(oEvent As Object) As Variant
    Dim oMenu As Object, oItem As Object
    Dim oSelSupp As Object, oSel As Variant, aRaw As Variant, nSheet As Long
    Dim i As Long, n As Long, bHasCut As Boolean, sCmd As String
    Dim sMode As String, bCellMode As Boolean, sKind As String
    Dim sBeforeTxt As String, sAfterTxt As String, sBeforeLow As String, sAfterLow As String
    Dim sCopy As String, sPaste As String, sCut As String, sMove As String
    Dim sErr As String, nLine As Long

    CMI_notifyContextMenuExecute = com.sun.star.ui.ContextMenuInterceptorAction.IGNORED
    On Error GoTo Oops

    oSelSupp = oEvent.Selection
    If IsNull(oSelSupp) Or IsEmpty(oSelSupp) Then Exit Function
    oSel = oSelSupp.getSelection()
    If IsNull(oSel) Or IsEmpty(oSel) Then Exit Function

    oMenu = oEvent.ActionTriggerContainer
    If IsNull(oMenu) Or IsEmpty(oMenu) Then Exit Function

    &apos; the menu of the sheet tabs: copy sheets and insert
    If IsSheetTabMenu(oMenu) Then
        If MenuHasOurEntries(oMenu) Then Exit Function
        If AddSheetEntries(oMenu, oSel) Then
            CMI_notifyContextMenuExecute = com.sun.star.ui.ContextMenuInterceptorAction.CONTINUE_MODIFIED
        End If
        Exit Function
    End If

    aRaw = ReadSelection(oSel, nSheet)       &apos; one range, or the ranges of a Ctrl selection
    If IsEmpty(aRaw) Then Exit Function

    &apos; already added by another registered interceptor?
    If MenuHasOurEntries(oMenu) Then Exit Function

    &apos; only touch menus that contain &quot;Cut&quot;
    For i = 0 To oMenu.Count - 1
        oItem = oMenu.getByIndex(i)
        sCmd = &quot;&quot;
        If Not IsNull(oItem) And Not IsEmpty(oItem) Then
            If oItem.PropertySetInfo.hasPropertyByName(&quot;CommandURL&quot;) Then
                sCmd = oItem.CommandURL
            End If
        End If
        If sCmd = &quot;.uno:Cut&quot; Then
            bHasCut = True
            Exit For
        End If
    Next i
    If Not bHasCut Then Exit Function

    &apos; --- what kind of selection is it? ---
    sMode = KindOfRanges(ThisComponent, nSheet, aRaw)
    If sMode = &quot;WHOLE&quot; Or sMode = &quot;MIXED&quot; Then Exit Function   &apos; nothing to offer
    bCellMode = (sMode = &quot;CELLS&quot;)
    If bCellMode Then
        sKind = &quot;cells&quot;
    ElseIf sMode = &quot;ROWS&quot; Then
        sKind = &quot;rows&quot;
        sBeforeTxt = Txt(&quot;dir.above&quot;) : sAfterTxt = Txt(&quot;dir.below&quot;)
        sBeforeLow = Txt(&quot;low.above&quot;) : sAfterLow = Txt(&quot;low.below&quot;)
    Else
        sKind = &quot;columns&quot;
        sBeforeTxt = Txt(&quot;dir.left&quot;) : sAfterTxt = Txt(&quot;dir.right&quot;)
        sBeforeLow = Txt(&quot;low.left&quot;) : sAfterLow = Txt(&quot;low.right&quot;)
    End If
    sCopy = Txt(&quot;m.copy.&quot; &amp; sKind)
    sPaste = Txt(&quot;m.paste.&quot; &amp; sKind)
    sCut = Txt(&quot;m.cut.&quot; &amp; sKind)
    sMove = Txt(&quot;m.move.&quot; &amp; sKind)

    n = 0
    If bCellMode Then
        If USE_SUBMENUS Then
            AddCellSubmenu oMenu, n, sCopy, &quot;StartCopy&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddCellSubmenu oMenu, n, sPaste, &quot;StartPasteSpecial&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddCellSubmenu oMenu, n, sCut, &quot;StartCut&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddCellSubmenu oMenu, n, sMove, &quot;StartMove&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuSeparator oMenu, n : n = n + 1
        Else
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sCopy &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; Txt(&quot;low.above&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartCopyAbove&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sCopy &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; Txt(&quot;low.below&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartCopyBelow&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sCopy &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; Txt(&quot;low.left&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartCopyLeft&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sCopy &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; Txt(&quot;low.right&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartCopyRight&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuSeparator oMenu, n : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sPaste &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; Txt(&quot;low.above&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartPasteSpecialAbove&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sPaste &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; Txt(&quot;low.below&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartPasteSpecialBelow&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sPaste &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; Txt(&quot;low.left&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartPasteSpecialLeft&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sPaste &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; Txt(&quot;low.right&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartPasteSpecialRight&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuSeparator oMenu, n : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sCut &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; Txt(&quot;low.above&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartCutAbove&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sCut &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; Txt(&quot;low.below&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartCutBelow&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sCut &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; Txt(&quot;low.left&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartCutLeft&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sCut &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; Txt(&quot;low.right&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartCutRight&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuSeparator oMenu, n : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sMove &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; Txt(&quot;low.above&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartMoveAbove&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sMove &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; Txt(&quot;low.below&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartMoveBelow&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sMove &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; Txt(&quot;low.left&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartMoveLeft&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sMove &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; Txt(&quot;low.right&quot;) &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartMoveRight&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuSeparator oMenu, n : n = n + 1
        End If
    Else
        If USE_SUBMENUS Then
            AddBeforeAfterSubmenu oMenu, n, sCopy, sBeforeTxt, sAfterTxt, &quot;StartCopyBefore&quot;, &quot;StartCopy&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddBeforeAfterSubmenu oMenu, n, sPaste, sBeforeTxt, sAfterTxt, &quot;StartPasteSpecialBefore&quot;, &quot;StartPasteSpecial&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddBeforeAfterSubmenu oMenu, n, sCut, sBeforeTxt, sAfterTxt, &quot;StartCutBefore&quot;, &quot;StartCut&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddBeforeAfterSubmenu oMenu, n, sMove, sBeforeTxt, sAfterTxt, &quot;StartMoveBefore&quot;, &quot;StartMove&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuSeparator oMenu, n : n = n + 1
        Else
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sCopy &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; sBeforeLow &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartCopyBefore&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sCopy &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; sAfterLow &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartCopy&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sPaste &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; sBeforeLow &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartPasteSpecialBefore&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sPaste &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; sAfterLow &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartPasteSpecial&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sCut &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; sBeforeLow &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartCutBefore&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sCut &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; sAfterLow &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartCut&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sMove &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; sBeforeLow &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartMoveBefore&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuItem oMenu, n, sMove &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; sAfterLow &amp; &quot;...&quot;, &quot;StartMove&quot; : n = n + 1
            AddMenuSeparator oMenu, n : n = n + 1
        End If
    End If

    CMI_notifyContextMenuExecute = com.sun.star.ui.ContextMenuInterceptorAction.CONTINUE_MODIFIED
    Exit Function

Oops:
    sErr = Error$ : nLine = Erl
    MsgBox Txt(&quot;err.menu&quot;) &amp; nLine &amp; Txt(&quot;err.sep&quot;) &amp; sErr, 16
    CMI_notifyContextMenuExecute = com.sun.star.ui.ContextMenuInterceptorAction.IGNORED
End Function

Sub CMI_disposing(oEvent As Object)
End Sub


&apos;=====================================================================
&apos;  2. Temporary document properties
&apos;     (they survive between the menu command and the callbacks)
&apos;=====================================================================
Sub SetDocProp(oDoc As Object, sName As String, sValue As String)
    Dim oProps As Object, bMod As Boolean
    bMod = oDoc.isModified()
    oProps = oDoc.DocumentProperties.UserDefinedProperties
    On Error Resume Next
    oProps.removeProperty(sName)
    On Error GoTo 0
    oProps.addProperty(sName, 128, sValue)      &apos; 128 = REMOVEABLE
    oDoc.setModified(bMod)
End Sub

Function GetDocProp(oDoc As Object, sName As String) As String
    Dim oProps As Object
    GetDocProp = &quot;&quot;
    On Error Resume Next
    oProps = oDoc.DocumentProperties.UserDefinedProperties
    GetDocProp = oProps.getPropertyValue(sName)
    On Error GoTo 0
End Function

Sub DelDocProp(oDoc As Object, sName As String)
    Dim oProps As Object, bMod As Boolean
    bMod = oDoc.isModified()
    On Error Resume Next
    oProps = oDoc.DocumentProperties.UserDefinedProperties
    oProps.removeProperty(sName)
    On Error GoTo 0
    oDoc.setModified(bMod)
End Sub

Sub SaveState(oDoc As Object, sValue As String)
    SetDocProp oDoc, STATE_NAME, sValue
End Sub

Function LoadState(oDoc As Object) As String
    LoadState = GetDocProp(oDoc, STATE_NAME)
End Function

Sub ClearState(oDoc As Object)
    DelDocProp oDoc, STATE_NAME
End Sub


&apos;=====================================================================
&apos;  3. Undo listener: after an Undo of one of our operations,
&apos;     select the source again
&apos;=====================================================================
&apos; An Undo happened
Sub UM_actionUndone(oEvent As Object)
    Dim oDoc As Object, oCtrl As Object, oSheet As Object
    Dim sTitle As String, sTopTitle As String, sInfo As String, sPref As String
    Dim a() As String

    On Error Resume Next
    sTitle = oEvent.UndoActionTitle
    sPref = UndoPrefix()
    oDoc = ThisComponent
    sInfo = &quot;&quot;

    If Left(sTitle, Len(sPref)) = sPref Then
        &apos; our copy / cut / move / paste special insertion was undone: select the original source
        sInfo = GetDocProp(oDoc, UNDO_NAME)
        DelDocProp oDoc, UNDO_NAME
        DelDocProp oDoc, PSSRC_NAME
    ElseIf GetDocProp(oDoc, PSSRC_NAME) &lt;&gt; &quot;&quot; Then
        &apos; a paste special is pending. If the step now on top of the Undo stack is our
        &apos; insertion, then the step just undone was the paste itself.
        sTopTitle = &quot;&quot;
        If oDoc.UndoManager.isUndoPossible() Then
            sTopTitle = oDoc.UndoManager.getCurrentUndoActionTitle()
        End If
        If Left(sTopTitle, Len(sPref)) = sPref Then
            sInfo = GetDocProp(oDoc, PSSRC_NAME)       &apos; the source where it sits right now
            DelDocProp oDoc, PSSRC_NAME
        End If
    End If
    If sInfo = &quot;&quot; Then Exit Sub

    If Left(sInfo, 2) = &quot;S|&quot; Then
        &apos; sheets: select the first source sheet again (that sheet only)
        Dim sRest As String, nAt As Long, sRg As String
        sRest = Mid(sInfo, 3)
        nAt = InStr(sRest, &quot;@&quot;)
        sRg = &quot;&quot;
        If nAt &gt; 0 Then
            sRg = Mid(sRest, nAt + 1)
            sRest = Left(sRest, nAt - 1)
        End If
        SelectFirstSheet oDoc, CLng(Split(sRest, &quot;,&quot;)(0)), sRg
        Exit Sub
    End If

    a = Split(sInfo, &quot;|&quot;)
    oCtrl = oDoc.CurrentController
    oSheet = oDoc.Sheets.getByIndex(CLng(a(0)))
    oCtrl.setActiveSheet(oSheet)
    &apos; a(1) holds all the source ranges: they are all selected again
    oCtrl.select(BuildSelection(oDoc, CLng(a(0)), StringToRanges(a(1))))
End Sub

